    "note": "Chapter 12 is sourced from the Junior Fastrack botany book (book pp.29-35), which prints the question and a model answer but NO star ranks and NO asked-year citations, so the missing stars/appearances record an absence of signal, not zero frequency. Only ONE source book is held for botany — the TSBIE Basic Learning Material on hand is physics-only and no botany board paper is in the corpus — so the two-book union check and the board-paper back-test are both STRUCTURALLY IMPOSSIBLE for this card, not merely pending. The mark split is authored, not printed. BOOK ERROR RECORDED: the printed answer states that the mesophyll 'contains either palisade or spongy parenchyma but not both'. That is wrong. In an isobilateral leaf the mesophyll is not differentiated into either kind; all the cells are alike. The card writes the correct version. The book also prints 'isobilatera' for isobilateral, 'similr' for similar and 'callateral' for collateral."
